  "reason": "The dominant finding from the 5 completed experiments is that scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder dramatically outperforms scgpt (0.706 vs ~0.52-0.54), making it the clear direction to exploit. The best config (config_045: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.706) leaves the aggregation method as an important untested variable for this RNA encoder. For scgpt, avgpool slightly beat transformer (0.542 vs 0.520), but scvi_n200 produces a fundamentally different latent representation that may interact differently with transformer-based aggregation. Config_021 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) is a clean single-variable change from the best config, testing whether transformer aggregation can push accuracy beyond 0.706. This is the highest-value next experiment: it either confirms avgpool is optimal (focusing remaining budget on other levers) or discovers a further improvement in the most promising configuration family."
}

